  "other_facts": "Coronary artery dimensions adjusted for body surface area and compared to 85 normal control subjects. Univariate analysis of pre-IVIG data showed significantly higher neutrophil count, CRP, total bilirubin, AST, ALT, and LDH in IVIG-non-responsive patients. Multivariate analysis selected CRP (p=0.009), total bilirubin (p<0.001), and AST (p=0.002) as independent predictors of non-responsiveness. Predictive criteria: at least two of CRP >=7.0 mg/dL, total bilirubin >=0.9 mg/dL, or AST >=200 IU/L define non-responsiveness. More intense initial therapy may be a promising strategy for predicted IVIG-non-responsive patients.",
