  "other_facts": "A novel and selective LC-MS/MS method was established and validated for simultaneous determination of subutinib and active metabolite in human urine. Urine samples were extracted by liquid-liquid extraction with ethyl acetate. Separation was on a Wondasil C18 column (150 × 2.1 mm, 3.5 µm) with mobile phase methanol-0.2% formic acid solution (73:27, v/v) at a flow rate of 0.2 mL/min. The linear range was 0.5000-200.0 ng/mL for both analytes, with a lower limit of quantitation of 0.5000 ng/mL. Intra- and inter-run precisions were <11.8% and <14.3%, respectively. Accuracies were <4.5% and <5.4% for the two analytes. Extraction recoveries were 88.8-97.5% and 93.8-99.4% for subutinib and active metabolite, respectively. Carryover values were <15% for both analytes. The method was applied to study urinary excretion of subutinib and active metabolite in humans after oral administration of subutinib maleate capsules in fed and fasting states.",
  "summary": "A novel LC-MS/MS method was validated for simultaneous determination of subutinib and its active metabolite in human urine and applied to study urinary excretion after oral administration of subutinib maleate capsules in fed and fasting states."
}

