  "other_facts": "Subgroup prevalence 2% (9/459). Median age of other 450 patients: 63 years (p<0.01). Somatic hypermutation and DNA replication repair deficiency due to biallelic inactivation of canonical mismatch repair gene. Germline heterozygous mutations in mismatch repair genes with somatic inactivation of remaining allele, consistent with Lynch syndrome. Subset with POLE proofreading domain mutations and resultant “ultrahypermutation”. Tumors lacked EGFR amplification, lacked combined trisomy 7/monosomy 10, only rarely had TERT promoter mutation or CDKN2A homozygous deletion. Frequent inactivating mutations in TP53, NF1, PTEN, ATRX, SETD2; recurrent activating mutations in PDGFRA. DNA methylation profiling revealed globally hypomethylated epigenomes and mostly classified as 'Diffuse pediatric-type high grade glioma, RTK1 subtype, subclass A'. Five patients treated with immune checkpoint blockade, four survived >3 years. The subtype is named 'De novo replication repair deficient glioblastoma, IDH-wildtype'.",
