  "other_facts": "Tests included M-mode and Doppler echocardiography, plasma BNP, and Hb measurements. Patients with atrial fibrillation or poor echocardiographic images were excluded. Confounding factors: diabetes mellitus, hypertension, age, HD duration, LV fractional shortening, E/A of transmitral flow velocity pattern, Tei index, LVMI, BNP level, Hb, and use of antihypertensive or antiarrhythmic drugs. Six CHF events occurred during mean follow-up of 1703+/-565 days. In univariate analysis, DM, LVMI, BNP, and Hb <10 g/dl were selected. In stepwise Cox regression, DM and Hb <10 g/dl were independent predictors. Time-dependent covariates analysis showed constant hazard over time (T_COV*DM p=0.726, T_COV*Hb <10 g/dl p=0.681).",
  "summary": "In 100 maintenance hemodialysis patients followed for a mean of 1703 days, diabetes mellitus and hemoglobin <10 g/dL independently predicted congestive heart failure events, while echocardiographic measures of cardiac function did not."
