  "other_facts": "Method: LC-MS/MS for biomonitoring of arsenic, benzene, and PAHs in human urine. Urinary metabolites: MMAA, DMAA, S-PMA, 1-OHP. Sample preparation: enzymatic deconjugation, 4 mL urine, 2-step extraction (1st: n-hexane with 10% ethyl acetate for 1-OHP; 2nd: chloroform/ammonium bicarbonate back-extraction for MMAA, DMAA, S-PMA). Extracts combined and analyzed by LC-MS/MS. Validation: spiked urine samples. Linear ranges (r²>0.99): MMAA 2-64 ng/mL, DMAA 1-64 ng/mL, S-PMA 0.78-100 ng/mL, 1-OHP 0.05-6.4 ng/mL. Accuracy (% Error): -16.67 to 29.17%. Precision (CV%): 2.03-30.99% (3 spiked levels, 6 replicates). Application: 10 real urine samples. Detected concentrations: MMAA BQL-8.38 ng/mL, DMAA BQL-10.71 ng/mL, S-PMA BQL-2.55 ng/mL, 1-OHP BQL-0.17 ng/mL, consistent with reported background levels.",
  "summary": "An LC-MS/MS method was developed and validated for simultaneous determination of urinary metabolites of arsenic, benzene, and PAHs (MMAA, DMAA, S-PMA, 1-OHP) with reported linearity, accuracy, and precision, and successfully applied to 10 real urine samples."
}

