  "other_facts": "Melatonin is a hormone that regulates the biological day and night cycle, mainly produced by the pineal gland during the night, and used as a soporific drug. The aim of the study was to develop a rapid quantification method for melatonin in hypnotics. The method used atmospheric pressure solid analysis probe-assisted mass spectrometry without chromatographic separation, with a single analysis taking less than 1 min. Reference measurements were performed with ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography coupled with a quadrupole-time-of-flight mass spectrometer. Both methods were validated and tested on real sample extracts. The two methods gave comparable results. The content of melatonin differed from the specified value in many samples.",
  "summary": "A rapid atmospheric pressure solid analysis probe mass spectrometry method was developed for quantifying melatonin in hypnotics, achieving coefficients of determination above 0.97, limits below 1 mg kg−1, and revealing deviations up to 78% from labeled values."
}

